; Test with-handlers with two lit handlers in sequence
; First handler adds 100, second handler adds 1000
; Due to nesting: (with-menv (set-meta! 'lit h1) (with-menv (set-meta! 'lit h2) body))
; The innermost h2 wins for the body, but h2 sees h1's lit when it calls default-handler
; Actually: the outer one comes first in the build, so:
; (with-handlers ((a h1) (b h2)) body) =>
; (with-menv (set-meta! 'a h1) (with-menv (set-meta! 'b h2) body))
; So h2 is the active one for 'b, and body runs in that context
; Let's just test two different handlers work:
(with-handlers
  ((lit (lambda (x) (+ 100 (default-handler 'lit x))))
   (if (lambda (x) (default-handler 'if x))))
  (+ 1 2))
